 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection in MATLAB, you can use the `imgaussfilt` function to apply the Gaussian filter and then use your existing code for Sobel edge detection. Here's how you can modify your code:
```
% Read input image and convert it to grayscale
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Apply Gaussian filter
gaussian_filtered_image = imgaussfilt(double(gray_image), 3); % 3 is the standard deviation of the Gaussian filter
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```
In this modified code, we first read the input image and convert it to grayscale as before. Then, we apply a Gaussian filter using the `imgaussfilt` function with a standard deviation of 3 pixels. After that, we define the Sobel operators and apply them to the gaussian_filtered_image instead of the original gray_image. Finally, we combine the edges in both directions and display the edge image.
This modification should help reduce the noise in the image before applying the Sobel edge detection.

