\title{Support Ticket: Technical Issue with Third-Party API Integration}
\author{}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section*{English Version}
\subsection*{Description of the Issue}
We are encountering a technical problem while integrating a third-party API into our multi-tiered system architecture. The error message displayed is: "API call failed with status code 403 Forbidden". The corresponding log entry reads: "Error connecting to API: [api\_url]: Error: connect ECONNREFUSED 123.45.67.89:80".

\subsection*{System Architecture}
\begin{table}[h!]
\centering
\caption{Multi-Tiered System Architecture}
\label{tab:architecture}
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}
\hline
Layer & Component & Description \\ \hline
Presentation & Web Application & User interface \\ \hline
Application & Business Logic & Processing logic \\ \hline
Integration & API Gateway & Third-party API integrator \\ \hline
Data & Database & Data storage \\ \hline
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\subsection*{Proposed Solution}
Based on our investigation, it appears that the issue may be caused by incorrect API credentials or an IP address restriction from the third-party provider. We propose the following steps to resolve this issue:

1. Verify that the API key and secret are correct and up-to-date.
2. Check if the IP address of our server is whitelisted by the third-party provider. If not, request access to their IP whitelist.
3. Implement retry mechanisms to handle transient errors.

\subsection*{Impact Analysis}
The impact of this issue is minimal at present, but could potentially affect system performance if the API calls fail frequently. Users may experience delays when interacting with affected features.

