 To create a simple toast notification using React and the useContext Hook, you can follow these steps: First, let's create a custom context for managing the toast messages.

1. Create a new file called `ToastContext.js`:

```javascript
import { createContext } from "react";

export const ToastContext = createContext();

export const ToastProvider = ({ children }) => {
  const [toasts, setToasts] = React.useState([]);

  const addToast = (message) => {
    setToasts((prevToasts) => [...prevToasts, message]);
    setTimeout(() => {
      setToasts((prevToasts) => prevToasts.filter((_, index) => index !== prevToasts.length - 1));
    }, 3000); // Duration of the toast notification
  };

  return (
    <ToastContext.Provider value={{ addToast }}>
      {children}
      {toasts.map((toast, index) => (
        <div key={index} className="toast">
          {toast}
        </div>
      ))}
    </ToastContext.Provider>
  );
};
```

2. Now, let's create a component that will display the toast notifications, `Toast.js`. This component will be a functional component and will consume the `ToastContext`:

